Now CSS. This is substantial. Need careful responsive design.

Let me define CSS variables and layout.

Colors:
--bg #06060a
--panel rgba(15,15,24,.88)
--line rgba(255,255,255,.08)
--txt #e8e8f0
--muted #8b8ba3
--lime #e8ff3f
--pink #ff3d81
--cyan #54e6ff
--red #ff4d5e

Fonts: `font-family: "Pretendard", "Noto Sans KR", "Apple SD Gothic Neo", "Malgun Gothic", system-ui, sans-serif;` Headings italic bold, letter-spacing.

Background: radial gradients, grid overlay fixed.

Layout:
body overflow hidden? On desktop game fits; mobile may need scroll. Use `html,body{height:100%}`; app min-height 100svh; allow overflow-y auto on small heights. For title screen fixed full.

`.game { display:flex; flex-direction:column; min-height:100svh; }`
header ~62px; stage flex:1 with grid columns 220px minmax(0,1fr) 260px; gap 14; padding 0 16; max-width 1500; margin auto; width 100%.
board-col flex column align center gap 8.
board-shell width min(100%, calc((100svh - 360px) * 7 / 8), 520px); aspect-ratio 7/8. If viewport height small, maybe minimum 320px. Use CSS clamp? `width: min(100%, 56vh, 520px)`? 56vh of 900 = 504; board height 576. Header 62 + roundbar 46 + board 576 + bench 64 + shop 170 = 918 too tall for 900. Need board height ≤ 100svh - 350 = 550 => width 481. So `width: min(100%, calc((100svh - 340px) * 0.875), 500px)`. At 800 height: 460*0.875=402 wide/459 high; total ~810. Slight. Use calc((100svh - 360px)*0.875) and min 318px? On 700 height: 340*.875=297 -> too small; mobile uses different layout.

For mobile (<900px), use different: board width min(94vw, calc((100svh - 330px)*0.875), 440px) with min maybe 280px. Shop 150. Mobile viewport 740: (410)*.875=359, 94vw=338 => 338. board height 386. Total: 56+40+40+386+52+150+? = 724. Tight but okay. Also hide side panels and reduce gaps.

I'd rather allow scrolling on mobile than squeeze. Body overflow-y auto. Use min-heights.

Let me construct with CSS grid areas:
```
.game{
 display:grid;
 grid-template-rows: auto 1fr auto;
}
.stage{display:grid;grid-template-columns:210px minmax(0,1fr) 270px;gap:12px;align-items:start;...}
```
board-col centered.

Shop: grid columns 170px 1fr; height ~168 desktop. cards 5 columns.

Mobile:
```
@media (max-width: 980px){
 .stage{grid-template-columns:1fr;}
 .panel-left{display:none}
 .panel-right{display:none}
 .hud{...}
 .shop{grid-template-columns:1fr; padding...}
 .shop-controls{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:6px}
 .shop-title{display:none}
 .shop-cards{overflow-x:auto;display:flex}
 .shop-card{min-width:104px}
 .board-shell{width:min(94vw, calc((100svh - 330px)*.875), 430px)}
}
```
Wait mobile synergy chips need visible; add a `#mobile-synergy`? I didn't include. Instead show left panel as horizontal strip on mobile: transform `.panel-left` to order and display block with `.synergy-list{display:flex;overflow-x:auto}` and hide panel tip; place it inside stage? Stage order: panel-left, board-col, panel-right. With grid single column, panel-left appears above board - good. Make compact height. And panel-right hidden. So keep panel-left visible in mobile as strip. `.panel-left{position:static}`.

Mobile order: stage -> panel-left (chips), board-col, panel-right hidden. Good.

HUD on mobile: brand shrink (hide subtitle), stats compact; hp/gold/lvl/streak 4 in row. Hud height maybe 54. Actions sound/help positioned. Level xp bar small.

Shop bottom fixed? Could be sticky bottom on mobile for reachability, but adds complexity; keep in flow. Ensure it doesn't cover.

Title screen CSS: full fixed, centered, background. Title logo huge with outline text: ZERO white, // lime, CHESS transparent with stroke? Use color #fff for ZERO, lime for CHESS. Big italic.

Character tiles decoration: `.title-agents` absolutely positioned cards around edges with gradient and initials, rotated, low opacity. JS populates 6.

Add glitch/hazard stripes.

Unit token CSS:
```css
.unit{position:absolute;width:calc(100%/7);height:calc(100%/8);padding:.35%;box-sizing:border-box;transition:left .18s linear, top .18s linear;z-index:5;touch-action:none;cursor:pointer}
.unit .u-card{position:relative;width:100%;height:100%;border-radius:22%;background:linear-gradient(150deg,var(--c1),var(--c2));border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.3);box-shadow:...;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;overflow:hidden}
.u-card::before{diagonal shine}
.u-face{font-weight:900;font-size:...; color:#fff;text-shadow}
.u-role{position:absolute;top:2%;right:4%;font-size:...}
.u-star{position:absolute;top:2%;left:4%;font-size...;color:#ffd23f;letter-spacing:-1px}
.u-name{position:absolute;bottom:16%;width:100%;text-align:center;font-size:...;background:rgba(0,0,0,.55)}
.u-bars{position:absolute;bottom:0;left:0;right:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1px;padding:2px 3px;}
```
Need dynamic font sizing based on board cell. Use CSS container queries? Set `--cell` via JS on board-shell as px from ResizeObserver, then font-size: calc(var(--cell)*0.34). Easier than cqw. But we can use cqw if `.unit` is container? Container queries units cqw refer to container. Make `.unit-layer{container-type:size}` and use `cqw`? cqw is % of container width. font-size: 8cqw -> for 480px board = 38px (too big for face maybe). Cell width 1/7 = 14.3% => 100/7 = 14.3cqw. Face ~7cqw = 33px at 480. Good. Name 2.5cqw ~12px. Bars height 1.6cqw. Use cqw units, widely supported modern browsers. Fallback: JS sets --cell and use calc(var(--cell, 52px)*X). I'll set `--cell` via ResizeObserver in JS and use that; simpler cross-browser.

Set on board-shell: style.setProperty('--cell', width/7 + 'px').

But bench also uses tokens; set --cell on bench too (slot width).

Token label: show 1 char face. Name label maybe only on prep? During combat it adds clutter. Show name plate always but small; okay.

HP bar `.u-hp` height calc(var(--cell)*0.055) min 3px; mana 2px.

Enemy tokens: `.unit.enemy .u-card{border-color: rgba(255,90,140,.5); filter...}` and glyph.

Dead: `.unit.dead{opacity:0; transform:scale(.4); transition...}` but left/top transitions conflict with transform; fine.

Casting: `.unit.casting .u-card{animation: castPulse .4s}`; hit flash.

Selected: `.unit.selected .u-card{outline:2px solid var(--lime); transform:translateY(-2px)}`. Note transform not used for positioning (left/top), so okay.

Valid cell: `.cell.valid::after{content:'';position:absolute;inset:6%;border:1px dashed rgba(232,255,63,.5);border-radius:8%;background:rgba(232,255,63,.06)}`.

Board cells:
```css
.board{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(7,1fr);grid-template-rows:repeat(8,1fr);width:100%;height:100%;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid ...;background:#0a0a12;}
