Now CSS for images. Need carefully layer.

Token:
```css
.unit .u-img {
 position:absolute; inset:4%; width:92%; height:92%;
 object-fit:cover; object-position:center 26%;
 border-radius:50%;
 z-index:2;
 pointer-events:none;
}
.unit .u-face { z-index:1; }
```
But circle icon has transparent corners; object-fit cover on 142 square; fine. Face hidden behind image but might peek in corners where icon transparent. The face is at center; image covers center, so no peek. Good.

`u-card::before` z-index 1 (shine). Image z2. Bars z4. Role z4. Name z4. Star z4.

Shop:
```css
.sc-img{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 20%;z-index:2;pointer-events:none}
.sc-face{z-index:1}
.sc-portrait::before/after currently no z-index, so they render after the img in painting order? Pseudo-elements ::before and ::after are children; with no z-index they stack in DOM order: ::before first, then img (z2), then ::after? ::after comes after img in generated order; if both z-auto, ::after paints above img, adding scanlines - nice. But ::after is a gradient overlay (scanlines) without z-index; img z2 would be above. Set overlays z3? The shine overlay should be above image. Add `z-index:3` to ::before/::after, pointer-events none. But `::after` scanlines on top of face. Good.
```
Currently `.sc-portrait::before` background gradient, `::after` scanlines. Set z-index 3.
`.shop-card::before` top border z3 already.

Bench:
```css
.bu-img{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 22%;z-index:1;border-radius:2px}
.bu-face{z-index:0? currently 1}
.bu-star z2; .bu-name z3; so image z1 behind name/star, face behind image.
```
But if face z1 and image z1, DOM order image before face → face above image. Set image z1, face z0? `.bu-face` position relative z-index 1. Change face z-index 1 and image z2, name z3. Fine.

Detail:
```css
.detail-face span {position:relative;z-index:1}
.detail-img{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 20%;z-index:2}
.detail-face::after (shine) currently no z-index; set z3 pointer-events none.
```
Image above shine? set shine z3.

Title:
```css
.t-img{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 15%;z-index:1}
.t-agent::after z-index:0
.t-agent::before z-index:2
.t-agent span z-index:3 (already position absolute no z; set z3)
```
Currently ::before gradient inset 0; set z2. ::after face; set z0. Then image z1 covers face. Good.

Sel bar:
```css
.sb-face{position:relative;overflow:hidden}
.sb-fallback{position:relative;z-index:0}
.sb-img{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 20%;z-index:1;border-radius:3px}
```

Also `.sc-img`, `.bu-img`, `.detail-img`, `.sb-img` use loading lazy? fine.

Character art backgrounds: For shop full art 283x307, object-fit cover in portrait area maybe crop chin; object-position center 15%. Good.

Face full art may include transparent background and a close-up; good.

Let's add CSS. Also `.fan-credit` style and title foot line-height.

Potential issue: `onerror="this.remove()"` inline attribute inside JS template string; valid.

Also **CSP** none.

Need ensure images loaded before screenshot; add `loading="lazy"` could delay offscreen; shop visible, loads. Tokens created on demand; fine. For title, lazy might delay; okay.

Add CSS.

